    <!-- base -->
    <string name="app_name">BentoBar fork</string>
    <string name="a11y_label">BentoBar fork</string>
    <string name="a11y_summary">Draws your items in the status bar</string>
    <string name="a11y_description">BentoBar draws your items (network speed, timer, calendar, tools…) on the status bar. Android allows that only through an accessibility service.\n\nWith it on, BentoBar: reads the status bar\'s layout, to find free space for your items; with the App menu bar on (Look), reads which app is in front (its package name) and the system\'s title bar over its window, to show that app\'s menus and press its title bar\'s buttons from the Window menu, and, when you start a quick action that only the launcher may start, the taskbar\'s icons (their names, which can include a window\'s title) to find that app\'s icon, and the menu it opens, and, when you add a widget from the Widgets menu, the launcher\'s widget list (its apps\' and widgets\' names), to open that app\'s page and press its Add for you; reads the color of the status bar clock, so your items match it; and runs the system actions you pick in the Tools menu or as a Shortcut item, such as screenshot or lock.\n\nIt never reads what other apps show inside their windows, and doesn\'t watch your keyboard, mouse or touches. Nothing the service reads ever leaves your Googlebook: BentoBar never collects or shares it.</string>
